# Keep this file private. On Linux: chmod 600 (control refuses to read a password
# from an .env other users can read, and never exports it to os.environ). On
# Windows scripts\install.ps1 sets the ACL to your account only; anything outside
# your user profile is flagged as not private.
#
# Linux only -- nothing on Windows needs elevation. Used by control.sudo to run
# the two setup helpers without an interactive prompt.
CONTROL_SUDO_PASSWORD="000923"

# Reject insecure .env files entirely instead of warning.
# CONTROL_ENV_STRICT=1

# Print JSON (including structured errors) for every command.
# CONTROL_JSON=1

# --- multi-agent (all optional) ---
# Act as this agent session: scopes window commands to its virtual desktop and
# uses its own browser profile. See "Running several agents in parallel" in README.
# CONTROL_SESSION_ID=agent_1

# Seconds to wait for another agent to finish sending input before giving up.
# CONTROL_INPUT_LOCK_TIMEOUT=30
# CONTROL_INPUT_LOCK=C:\Users\you\AppData\Local\Temp\control_input.lock

# JSON file with extra/overriding selectors for `control browser ask` (see README).
# CONTROL_AI_SITES=C:\path\to\ai-sites.json

# --- Windows only ---
# Interpreters to try first for the AT-SPI worker. Ignored on Windows, where
# `control a11y` answers in-process through UI Automation.
# CONTROL_ATSPI_PYTHON=/usr/bin/python3
